  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\hat{\\mathbf{i}}+\\hat{\\mathbf{j}}+\\hat{\\mathbf{k}}, \\mathbf{b}=\\hat{\\mathbf{i}}-\\hat{\\mathbf{j}}+\\hat{\\mathbf{k}}$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\hat{\\mathbf{i}}-\\hat{\\mathbf{j}}-\\hat{\\mathbf{k}}$ be three vectors. A vector $\\mathbf{v}$ in the plane of $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ whose projection of $\\mathbf{c}$ is $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$, is given by"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\hat{\\mathbf{i}}-3 \\hat{\\mathbf{j}}+3 \\hat{\\mathbf{k}}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-3 \\hat{\\mathbf{i}}-3 \\hat{\\mathbf{j}}-\\hat{\\mathbf{k}}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$3 \\hat{\\mathbf{i}}-\\hat{\\mathbf{j}}+3 \\hat{\\mathbf{k}}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\hat{\\mathbf{i}}+3 \\hat{\\mathbf{k}}-3 \\hat{\\mathbf{k}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathbf{v}=\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda \\mathbf{b}$\n$$\n\\mathbf{v}=(1+\\lambda) \\hat{\\mathbf{i}}+(1-\\lambda) \\hat{\\mathbf{j}}+(1+\\lambda) \\hat{\\mathbf{k}}\n$$\nProjection of $\\mathbf{v}$ on $\\mathbf{c}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\n$$\n\\begin{array}{lc}\n\\Rightarrow & \\frac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{c}}{|\\mathbf{c}|}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\frac{(1+\\lambda)-(1-\\lambda)-(1+\\lambda)}{\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & 1+\\lambda-1+\\lambda-1-\\lambda=1 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\lambda-1=1 \\Rightarrow \\lambda=2 \\\\\n\\therefore & \\mathbf{v}=3 \\hat{\\mathbf{i}}-\\hat{\\mathbf{j}}+3 \\hat{\\mathbf{k}}\n\\end{array}\n$$"
  }
}